                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "98caed88-cf20-372c-a5f8-f8a2538d713f",
                        "entry_id": "7896ecc8-89fb-373e-9797-116200f24f62",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To awaken, arouse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3482afb-bfd1-49b2-8080-bbc02e3a5b4e",
                                "sense_id": "98caed88-cf20-372c-a5f8-f8a2538d713f",
                                "text": "And hir awook, and thus to hir he cried, \"Woman, what is that, that in thin hand I see? What hast thou doon, woman, for him that diede, What wickid spirit hath travaylid the?\" And as sone as that adawed was she, The knyfe fel oute of hir hand in the bedde, And she bihilde the cloothis al forbledde, And the childe dead."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8324a2d-c9c2-4bac-a0be-c3a64f154116",
                                "sense_id": "98caed88-cf20-372c-a5f8-f8a2538d713f",
                                "text": "The soulles body about the bed did sprall, / While they about it on the King did call, / Adawing him as if he wer in swound: / But all for nought, he had his deadly wound."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1215655d-972a-4dad-8294-1bab27b5a349",
                                "sense_id": "98caed88-cf20-372c-a5f8-f8a2538d713f",
                                "text": "To arrive to knowledge is to have an itinerary, a passage out of dreaming, to adaw, to be awake (délit)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
